00:50:54.600 --> 00:50:57.760
and it will select
and use appropriate data sets.

00:50:57.760 --> 00:51:01.800
In our case,
this is the case filings.

00:51:01.800 --> 00:51:02.920
Correct.

00:51:02.920 --> 00:51:05.800
Now, we need to set
the correct options again

00:51:05.800 --> 00:51:08.720
to provide reference
to the history.

00:51:10.640 --> 00:51:11.800
We're going to be able

00:51:11.800 --> 00:51:14.280
to call the variance
across the entire reference.

00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:15.680
But there is an option

00:51:15.680 --> 00:51:20.040
to specify
just some subset of the regions.

00:51:20.040 --> 00:51:24.400
We're going to call assemblies
and insertions deletions.

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:29.680
We're going to set
some additional options.

00:51:29.680 --> 00:51:34.920
We're going to say that we want
as the minimum coverage 50,

00:51:34.920 --> 00:51:39.120
so meaning sites that have less
than 50 leads

00:51:39.120 --> 00:51:41.240
will not be uncovered.

00:51:41.240 --> 00:51:43.240
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:51:52.600 --> 00:51:56.600
So this setting is important
to make sure

00:51:56.600 --> 00:52:02.520
that you're not calling
ambiguous alignments.

00:52:02.520 --> 00:52:04.200
And...

00:52:07.200 --> 00:52:09.400
We are going to say...

00:52:09.400 --> 00:52:12.680
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:52:12.680 --> 00:52:14.520
So, again, these are settings

