00:52:49.120 --> 00:52:53.480
So that actually has
integrations for IGB,

00:52:53.480 --> 00:52:58.000
for Trexster,

00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:02.920
for JBrowse, and others.

00:53:02.920 --> 00:53:04.400
And it's also very easy.

00:53:04.400 --> 00:53:08.560
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:53:08.560 --> 00:53:12.640
Okay. So the next step is
that we will run [inaudible]

00:53:12.640 --> 00:53:16.840
which is a tool that
looks at the variant

00:53:16.840 --> 00:53:22.120
and predicts what, in fact,
the variant actually has.

00:53:28.520 --> 00:53:31.480
Okay. And there are tools
with variants.

00:53:31.480 --> 00:53:34.520
So there is a special version
just for SARS-CoV-2,

00:53:34.520 --> 00:53:37.600
which takes care of the multiple
overlapping living things

00:53:37.600 --> 00:53:40.560
that are inside the genome.

00:53:40.560 --> 00:53:42.240
So we're gonna use this one.

00:53:44.400 --> 00:53:50.000
As import, we need to select
the BCF file we just generated.

00:53:50.000 --> 00:53:51.720
It is BCF format.

00:53:51.720 --> 00:53:54.280
The genome is already correct.

00:53:54.280 --> 00:53:57.440
We want to create
a BCF again.

00:53:57.440 --> 00:54:01.840
We also...Sorry.
Is that correct?

